  "Gap attribution (VIX, SVI-cal surface): replicated - official = +1.04. Strikes beyond the stored strip would add +0.05 under the surface's wing; the stored quotes beyond the fitted K/F 0.70-1.30 are 0.58 index points richer than that wing, so the truncation figure likely understates. Inside the fitted range market and surface differ by +0.12 (these two terms set the replication against the surface; they are not part of the gap). Left unexplained by the chain: -1.09 (official - replicated - truncation; 105% of official - replicated): snapshot timing vs the 16:15 ET print, stale quotes."
